  },
  {
    question: "Can you build a website in English and Spanish?",
    answer: "Yes. Each language gets its own URLs, correct lang attributes, en-US and es-US hreflang tags, translated titles and structured data, and a switcher that keeps visitors on the equivalent page. We do not rely on browser translation for pages you want to rank. The Spanish copy comes from you or a translator you trust; we handle the build and test both versions.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can you guarantee a first-page ranking on Google?",
    answer: "No, and be wary of anyone who does. Nobody controls Google's results. We commit to a technically sound site, pages built around what your customers actually search, honest monthly reporting from Search Console, and steady improvement based on that data. Competitive US markets typically take three to six months or more to show real movement.",
  },
  {
    question: "Where will my website be hosted?",
